{
  "heading": "Lifecycle and events: Yon",
  "axis": "language",
  "summary": "One route, two shared services and a controller. CheckoutService publishes through the injected applicationEventPublisher during OnStart and releases in OnStop. AuditService holds the listeners. EventPublisher is removed (ADR 0031), and any use of it fails the build. So publishing is always a call on that field. Needs binds a Yon resource by the field's own name, which is the name Spring uses: dataSource, redisTemplate and applicationEventPublisher in every Yon language. Python and Rust write the field name in snake_case, so they bind the publisher by type. F# takes the publisher as a primary constructor parameter, so it binds it by type too. A listener takes exactly one parameter, and the model type of that parameter is the event it hears (ADR 0055). Order runs the listeners of one event from the lowest value first. condition skips delivery without an error. When a listener returns a model, Tachyon publishes that model as its own event, so the SettledOrder that settle returns reaches the next listener. InBackground appears only in JavaScript, TypeScript and Python. PHP, Java, Groovy, Kotlin, C#, F#, Rust, Dart, Go, Ruby and Lua have no asynchronous method here, and they reject it at compile time. GET /lifecycle answers with the recorded log and the final total. Ruby creates its publisher with ApplicationEventPublisher.new and names each listener's model in a YARD tag, # @param order [PlacedOrder]. Lua writes each hook as a comment marker above its method, such as `-- @OnStart` or `-- @OnEvent({\"id\":\"audit-log\"})`, names the listener's model in a LuaCATS tag, `---@param order PlacedOrder`, and publishes a model table, `setmetatable({ status = \"paid\", total = 25 }, PlacedOrder)`, through its `application_event_publisher = nil` field, which Tachyon binds by that name (ADR 0085). Lua has no asynchronous methods, so InBackground stops the build there too. A Lua model marked `-- @Topic` is a topic like in the other languages. C++ has no tab here, because C++ Yon code has only route controllers so far: the build refuses `Service` in C++ with `TY1308` (ADR 0099).",
